# Definition of Done

Before reporting a coding task as finished, verify these – do not just claim them:

## Verify (run the commands, don't assume)

- **Type check / build**: API `npm run build --prefix apps/api`; Web `npm run build --prefix apps/web`
- **Lint**: `npm run lint` (root) – zero errors, no new warnings
- **Tests**: `npm test` – all green; add/adjust tests for new logic (parsers, validators, services, components)

## Code quality

- No `any` – use `unknown` + type guard
- Explicit return types on public functions
- Code comments in English (see `comments-english`)
- New public functions/methods have TSDoc; new endpoints have `@openapi`

## Project specifics

- Version inputs validated via `isValidVersionInput()` before any nvm call
- Angular templates meet WCAG 2.1 AA (see `a11y` rule)
- `CHANGELOG.md` updated under `[Unreleased]` for user/developer-relevant changes

## When something fails

State it explicitly. Never silently skip a failing step or mark a task done with red tests.
If a step cannot be run (e.g. environment limitation), say so clearly instead of assuming success.
